---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>{SITE_TITLE}</h1>
			<p>
				I think and I code things. Most days these are mutually exclusive.
			</p>
			<p>
				In March I wrote one blog post. It was about how AI tools don't democratize outcomes, and I
				wrote it in the voice of someone accepting an award nobody had offered. Then I didn't post
				again for six months. In October I reread it and rewrote it so it would stop looking at me
				like that.
			</p>
			<p>
				The second post is about my keyboard's dead i key. I fixed it with a dictionary autocorrect
				that turned "done" into "dine" thirteen times, then wrote a script to replace that one, then
				wrote a key counter to keep an eye on the replacement. A new keyboard was also an option.
			</p>
			<p>
				By day I process GNSS data for geohazard assessments, where taking things seriously is the
				job. Everywhere else I do it by accident, and this blog is where I find out.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you're here for hype, wrong address. If you're here to watch someone build a metaphor
				about a hammer and then apologize for it two sentences later, welcome home.
			</p>
			<p>
				<a href="/blog">Read the evidence →</a>
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
